  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Signed, Sealed, Delivered**: rare: 7 archived performances [5]\n- **For My Friends**: rare: 3 archived performances [5]\n- **Love Having You Around**: mythic rare: 2 archived performances [5]\n- **My Baby Specializes**: rare: 3 archived performances [5]\n- **Baby I Do Love You**: rare: 3 archived performances [5]\n- **With A Little Help From My Friends**: rare: 3 archived performances [5]\n- **Papa Was A Rolling Stone *@$**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [5]\n- **Licking Stick *@$**: rare: 7 archived performances [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2012-05-03.mk4.flac16** (recommended): audience recording; 16 songs; 137 min; rated 4/5 by 2 [1]\n- **soulive2012-05-03.mk4.flac24**: audience recording; 16 songs; 137 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Show was the Royal Family Ball, sponsored by Jam Cruise, with Alan Evans Trio, Nigel Hall Band, Soulive, then Lettuce [1]\n- Shady Horns (Eric Bloom, James Casey, Ryan Zoidis) joined on some songs; Igmar Thomas and Jennifer Hartswick added trumpets [1]\n- Big Sam on trombone, Ivan Neville on keys and vocals, and Roosevelt Collier on lap steel joined the closing songs [1]\n- Show was the Royal Family Ball, sponsored by Jam Cruise, with Alan Evans Trio, Nigel Hall Band, Soulive, then Lettuce [2]\n- Guests included the Shady Horns, plus Igmar Thomas and Jennifer Hartswick on trumpet [2]\n- Big Sam, Ivan Neville and Roosevelt Collier sat in on trombone, keys/vocals and lap steel respectively [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2012-05-03.mk4.flac16**: taped by Eric McRoberts; transferred by Eric McRoberts; source: Audience/FOH [1]. Also: A higher quality 24 bit version of this audience recording is also available [1]\n- **soulive2012-05-03.mk4.flac24**: taped by Eric McRoberts; transferred by Eric McRoberts; source: Audience/FOH [2]. Also: This 24 bit version is not meant for MP3 streaming or CD burning; a 16 bit version exists [2]",
